{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-title",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Basira AI — 00: Colab Bootstrap\n",
    "\n",
    "**Run this notebook first at the start of every Colab session.**\n",
    "It mounts Google Drive, clones / pulls the repo, installs dependencies,\n",
    "confirms the GPU, and prints image counts for every dataset.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Privacy rule:** never paste Kaggle tokens or patient data into this notebook.\n",
    "> Never print or store API keys."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 1 — Mount Google Drive\n",
    "\n",
    "Persistent outputs (checkpoints, reports, figures) are saved to\n",
    "`/content/drive/MyDrive/basira/` so they survive session resets."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-mount-drive",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "import pathlib\n",
    "\n",
    "# Create output directories on Drive if they do not exist yet.\n",
    "DRIVE_ROOT = pathlib.Path('/content/drive/MyDrive/basira')\n",
    "for subdir in ('checkpoints', 'reports', 'figures'):\n",
    "    (DRIVE_ROOT / subdir).mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'Drive mounted. Output root: {DRIVE_ROOT}')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step2",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 2 — Clone or pull the Basira AI repo\n",
    "\n",
    "Replace `REPO_URL` with your actual GitHub URL.\n",
    "If the repo already exists in `/content/basira-ai`, we pull instead of cloning."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-clone-repo",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import os\n",
    "import subprocess\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Set your repo URL here ────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "REPO_URL  = 'https://github.com/Reticentain/basira-ai'   # <-- update this\n",
    "REPO_DIR  = pathlib.Path('/content/basira-ai')\n",
    "BRANCH    = 'main'\n",
    "# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "\n",
    "def run(cmd, **kwargs):\n",
    "    \"\"\"Run a shell command and print its output.\"\"\"\n",
    "    result = subprocess.run(cmd, shell=True, capture_output=True, text=True, **kwargs)\n",
    "    if result.stdout:\n",
    "        print(result.stdout.strip())\n",
    "    if result.returncode != 0 and result.stderr:\n",
    "        print('STDERR:', result.stderr.strip())\n",
    "    return result\n",
    "\n",
    "if REPO_DIR.exists():\n",
    "    print(f'Repo already exists at {REPO_DIR} — pulling latest changes...')\n",
    "    run(f'git -C {REPO_DIR} pull origin {BRANCH}')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print(f'Cloning {REPO_URL} ...')\n",
    "    run(f'git clone --branch {BRANCH} {REPO_URL} {REPO_DIR}')\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add repo root to Python path so `import basira` works.\n",
    "import sys\n",
    "SRC_DIR = str(REPO_DIR / 'src')\n",
    "if SRC_DIR not in sys.path:\n",
    "    sys.path.insert(0, SRC_DIR)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nRepo dir: {REPO_DIR}')\n",
    "run(f'git -C {REPO_DIR} log --oneline -5')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step3",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 3 — Install dependencies\n",
    "\n",
    "`torch` and `torchvision` are **not** in `requirements-colab.txt`;\n",
    "Colab already ships the GPU-optimised build — reinstalling would break it."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-install-deps",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "req_file = REPO_DIR / 'requirements-colab.txt'\n",
    "print(f'Installing from {req_file} ...')\n",
    "run(f'pip install -q -r {req_file}')\n",
    "print('Installation complete.')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 4 — Check GPU and log environment"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-check-gpu",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import torch\n",
    "import platform\n",
    "import random\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── GPU check ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n",
    "cuda_ok = torch.cuda.is_available()\n",
    "device  = torch.device('cuda' if cuda_ok else 'cpu')\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 55)\n",
    "print(f'  Python     : {platform.python_version()}')\n",
    "print(f'  PyTorch    : {torch.__version__}')\n",
    "print(f'  CUDA avail : {cuda_ok}')\n",
    "if cuda_ok:\n",
    "    print(f'  GPU        : {torch.cuda.get_device_name(0)}')\n",
    "    print(f'  VRAM       : {torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).total_memory / 1e9:.1f} GB')\n",
    "print(f'  Device     : {device}')\n",
    "print('=' * 55)\n",
    "\n",
    "if not cuda_ok:\n",
    "    print('\\n⚠️  No GPU detected. Training will be very slow.')\n",
    "    print('   Runtime → Change runtime type → T4 GPU')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 5 — Load config and set global random seeds"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-load-config",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from basira.config import load_config, print_config\n",
    "\n",
    "cfg = load_config()\n",
    "print_config(cfg)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ── Set global random seeds (log them so runs are reproducible) ───────────────\n",
    "SEED = cfg.seeds.global_seed\n",
    "random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "np.random.seed(SEED)\n",
    "torch.manual_seed(SEED)\n",
    "if cuda_ok:\n",
    "    torch.cuda.manual_seed_all(SEED)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(f'\\nGlobal seed set to {SEED} (cfg.seeds.global_seed).')"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 6 — Check dataset presence and count images\n",
    "\n",
    "This cell compares each dataset's image count and CSV row count against\n",
    "expected numbers, reading all paths from `cfg`, and prints OK or CHECK per dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-count-images",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pathlib\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "\n",
    "def count_images(folder: str | pathlib.Path, exts=('.jpg', '.jpeg', '.png')) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Count image files in a folder (non-recursive).\"\"\"\n",
    "    p = pathlib.Path(folder)\n",
    "    if not p.exists():\n",
    "        return -1\n",
    "    return sum(1 for f in p.iterdir() if f.suffix.lower() in exts)\n",
    "\n",
    "def count_csv_rows(csv_path: str | pathlib.Path) -> int:\n",
    "    \"\"\"Count rows in a CSV file.\"\"\"\n",
    "    p = pathlib.Path(csv_path)\n",
    "    if not p.exists():\n",
    "        return -1\n",
    "    return len(pd.read_csv(p))\n",
    "\n",
    "expected = {\n",
    "    'APTOS 2019': {\n",
    "        'images': cfg.data.aptos.images,\n",
    "        'csv': cfg.data.aptos.labels_csv,\n",
    "        'exp_images': 3662,\n",
    "        'exp_csv': 3662,\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'EyePACS train': {\n",
    "        'images': cfg.data.eyepacs.train_images,\n",
    "        'csv': cfg.data.eyepacs.train_labels,\n",
    "        'exp_images': 35126,\n",
    "        'exp_csv': 35126,\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'EyePACS test': {\n",
    "        'images': cfg.data.eyepacs.test_images,\n",
    "        'csv': cfg.data.eyepacs.test_labels,\n",
    "        'exp_images': 53576,\n",
    "        'exp_csv': 53576,\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'Messidor-2': {\n",
    "        'images': cfg.data.messidor2.images,\n",
    "        'csv': cfg.data.messidor2.labels_csv,\n",
    "        'exp_images': 1744,\n",
    "        'exp_csv': 1744,\n",
    "    },\n",
    "    'IDRiD': {\n",
    "        'images': cfg.data.idrid.images,\n",
    "        'csv': cfg.data.idrid.labels_csv,\n",
    "        'exp_images': 516,\n",
    "        'exp_csv': 516,\n",
    "    },\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "print('Dataset validation (images & CSV rows)')\n",
    "print('=' * 75)\n",
    "\n",
    "all_ok = True\n",
    "for name, spec in expected.items():\n",
    "    n_img = count_images(spec['images'])\n",
    "    n_csv = count_csv_rows(spec['csv'])\n",
    "    \n",
    "    img_match = (n_img == spec['exp_images'])\n",
    "    csv_match = (n_csv == spec['exp_csv'])\n",
    "    status = 'OK' if (img_match and csv_match) else 'CHECK'\n",
    "    if status == 'CHECK':\n",
    "        all_ok = False\n",
    "        \n",
    "    print(f\"  {name:<15} : images {n_img:>5}/{spec['exp_images']} | CSV {n_csv:>5}/{spec['exp_csv']} -> [{status}]\")\n",
    "\n",
    "print('=' * 75)\n",
    "if all_ok:\n",
    "    print('All datasets verified: OK')\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    print('⚠️  Some dataset counts do not match expected values. Please review items marked [CHECK].')\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "md-step7",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Step 7 — Run the patient-split integrity tests\n",
    "\n",
    "This runs `tests/test_patient_split.py` on synthetic data to confirm the\n",
    "leakage guard works before we touch any real data."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "cell-run-tests",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "run(f'python -m pytest {REPO_DIR}/tests/test_patient_split.py -v --tb=short')"
   ]
  },
  {
